node_modules/
# ...and any SIDECAR COPY of it. `node_modules/` matches that exact name only, so
# a repair/rollback backup like `node_modules.bak.wi5769/` is NOT ignored — and
# git-sync auto-commits the whole tree, so one such directory tries to push
# ~100k files and trips the GitHub 100MB blob limit (observed 2026-07-25: a
# concurrent-install repair left node_modules.bak.wi5769/, and git-sync had to
# exclude @cloudflare/workerd's 118MB binary from the auto-commit). Taking a
# backup before a risky reinstall is the RIGHT instinct — this just makes it safe.
node_modules.bak*/
node_modules.old*/
.next/
.next-prod/
.next-build-cache/

# Vitest scratch TMPDIR. Agents + the green-checkpoint run vitest with
# TMPDIR=$PWD/.vitest-tmp (the documented ENOENT workaround when the real TMPDIR
# is unwritable). Those are throwaway temp + node-compile-cache files — never
# source. Tracking them churned 8500+ junk files into the shared tree, spawned
# noise "should not commit" auto-commits, and slowed git-sync (WI-679). Ignore
# everywhere they land (root, packages/*, apps/*).
.vitest-tmp/
**/.vitest-tmp/
# Stray nested lockfiles (workspace members must ride the root lock) stay
# ignored, but the ROOT lockfile is the npm-ci source of truth for CI +
# fresh clones (regenerated + validated 2026-06-11, audit P-024/EI-84) —
# ignoring it meant CI had no lockfile and `npm ci` could never run.
package-lock.json
!/package-lock.json
*.tsbuildinfo
.DS_Store
*.log

# Vitest coverage output (published as CI artifacts, never committed — spec §1.13)
coverage/
**/coverage/

# Per-run test output (p2p-perf bench artifacts + report.md, Playwright, etc.).
# Ephemeral, keyed by a timestamp/runId — NOT source. Committed baselines that
# ARE source live elsewhere (e.g. perf/baselines/*.json) and are unaffected.
# (2026-06-07: git-sync was sweeping p2p-perf run dirs into commits.)
test-results/
**/test-results/
.env
.env.local
.source/

# Rust/Tauri build artifacts — accidentally committed before; never again.
# (2026-06-05: apps/{tui,pui-zellij-plugin,pui-companion-proto}/target/ got swept
# into git-sync commits — 10GB of unpushed >100MB blobs wedged the push for 20h.)
apps/*/target/
apps/operator-mobile/src-tauri/target/
# per-work-item isolated cargo target dirs (CARGO_TARGET_DIR=.wiNNNN-cargo-target):
# 2026-07-09 git-sync excluded a 240MB blob from .wi3388-cargo-target/ every sweep
.wi*-cargo-target/
*cargo-target*/
# Sidecar backup dirs left by desktop packaging (2026-07-10: git-sync excluded a
# 100.1MB node binary from papercusp-desktop/src-tauri/sidecar.old.55111/ every
# sweep — same class as the cargo-target churn above; never source).
sidecar.old*/
**/sidecar.old*/

# operator-docs (Astro+Starlight)
apps/operator-docs/dist/
apps/operator-docs/.astro/
# DOCS_PREVIEW (P-005 projection site): preview build out-dir + the generated
# lib-API markdown starlight-typedoc writes into the content tree. Both are
# projected from code on demand — never committed.
apps/operator-docs/dist-preview/
apps/operator-docs/src/content/docs/preview/

# papercusp-docs (Astro+Starlight)
apps/papercusp-docs/dist/
apps/papercusp-docs/.astro/

# tooldef family — src-as-entry; `build` (tsc) emits dist/ but nothing consumes it
packages/tooldef/dist/
packages/tooldef-http/dist/
packages/tooldef-mcp/dist/

# Per-spawn MCP config written into a harness cwd by console-launch /
# bootstrap-role (SU + role sessions). For the `papercup` harness that cwd IS
# this main checkout, and the file carries a SIGNED, time-limited MCP URL — it
# must never be committed (paperclip's `git add -A` would otherwise leak the
# credential). Was historically tracked then deleted; this closes the re-leak
# hole. `.papercusp.bak` is the backup console-launch makes of a pre-existing one.
.mcp.json
.mcp.json.papercusp.bak

# Rendered plan markdown — plans are PG-canonical; these .md are a DERIVED,
# read-only projection (rendered by `plans:export` for human reading), never the
# source of truth. Tracking them is the PG-mirror anti-pattern + constant churn
# (293 plans × many agents editing = a .md diff on every plan edit). Edits go via
# the plans tools, not these files. (2026-06-06: a full `plans:export --toDir`
# materialized all 293; this keeps them local-and-readable but out of git.)
apps/operator/docs/plans/**/*.md

# On-demand generated API projections (docs-and-memory-as-projections P-004):
# NOT committed by design — they cold-import the full tool registry / re-doc
# every lib export, so a committed copy churns on every tool or export change
# fleet-wide. Regenerate with `npm run gen:openapi` / `npm run gen:lib-api`.
.papercusp/openapi.json
.papercusp/lib-api/

# Gate-owned frozen-candidate repair worktrees are linked checkouts, never source.
# Without this rule git-sync's blanket add records the checkout itself as a mode-160000
# gitlink. The next candidate then inherits that undeclared gitlink and recursive git
# commands fail with "No url found ... in .gitmodules" (WI-39450).
.papercusp/worktrees/

# git-sync-embedded-repo-strand fix (2026-06-30, joint w/ 2b1a8 / WI-1354): transient test-scratch
# dirs that get a nested .git (an embedded repo). When ANY has NO commit checked out, `git add -A`
# FATALs (exit 128) → stages nothing → the whole tree strands uncommitted silently. Ignore ALL the
# tmp roots the lockdom/flg-repo/green-checkpoint/commit-reproject tests use in-repo. (git-sync also
# now excludes-and-retries on the fatal — run-git-sync.ts — so this is defense-in-depth.)
.vitest-tmp/
.vitest-tmpdir/
**/.vitest-tmp/
**/.vitest-tmpdir/
**/vitest-tmp/
.papercusp/vitest-tmp/
.papercusp/scratch/
**/scratch/relgit-*/
**/scratch/lockdom-*/

# WI-4419 (2026-07-12): a gitignore pattern containing a slash is ANCHORED to the
# directory of the .gitignore holding it — so `.papercusp/scratch/` above matches
# ONLY <repo-root>/.papercusp/scratch/. Agent state dirs also appear NESTED
# (packages/operator-core/.papercusp/, apps/operator/.papercusp/, ...), where the
# anchored patterns miss them — and git-sync auto-commits the whole tree, so what
# the pattern misses is committed automatically. That is how 529 scratch files and
# a live hyperbee LevelDB (whose LOG embeds the build box's home path + hostname)
# came to be TRACKED, and thence swept into every release bundle by the sidecar glob.
# These `**/` twins are the depth-matching guard (same fix already applied to
# .vitest-tmp above). Untracking what is ALREADY committed is separate — see WI-4419.
**/.papercusp/scratch/
**/.papercusp/vitest-tmp/
**/.papercusp/tmp/
**/.papercusp/tmp-*/
**/.papercusp/logs/
**/.papercusp/bench-reports/
**/.papercusp/pi-sessions/

# npm-only repo — a pnpm/yarn install breaks the shared node_modules layout (2026-07-03 fleet incident)
pnpm-lock.yaml
yarn.lock
.pnpm-workspace-state-v1.json

# WI-2911 (2026-07-05): ~1.85GB of never-source content was tracked into the shared
# tree — the bulk of `git archive HEAD` and of the release seed bundle. Untracked
# index-only (files stay on disk); these entries keep it from re-entering.
# Agent scratch/temp under .papercusp (scratch/ + vitest-tmp/ already ignored above).
.papercusp/tmp/
.papercusp/tmp-*/
.papercusp/logs/
.papercusp/bench-reports/
.papercusp/pi-sessions/
# Derived voice-runtime assets — copied out of node_modules by apps/operator's
# postinstall (scripts/setup-{vad,wake}-runtime.sh); every fresh install regenerates.
apps/operator/public/vad-runtime/
apps/operator/public/wake-runtime/
apps/operator/public/ort-wasm-*
apps/operator/public/silero_vad_*.onnx
apps/operator/public/vad.worklet.bundle.min.js
# Derived vditor runtime asset mirror (WI-7088) — copied out of node_modules by
# apps/operator's postinstall + operator-vite's prebuild
# (scripts/setup-vditor-runtime.sh). Serving these locally is what stops every
# cold markdown render fetching ~4.9MB from unpkg.com; ~23MB, regenerated on
# every fresh install, never committed.
apps/operator/public/vditor/
# Derived monaco-editor runtime asset mirror (cdn-egress-fixes-2026-08-02 P-001)
# — copied out of node_modules by apps/operator's postinstall + operator-vite's
# prebuild (scripts/setup-monaco-runtime.sh). Serving these locally is what stops
# every first Monaco mount fetching ~4MB (~11MB with the TS worker) from
# cdn.jsdelivr.net, AND what stops the app running 0.55.1 while we install
# 0.56.0; ~24MB, regenerated on every fresh install, never committed.
apps/operator/public/monaco/
# Derived excalidraw runtime asset mirror (cdn-egress-fixes-2026-08-02 P-004) —
# copied out of node_modules by apps/operator's postinstall + operator-vite's
# prebuild (scripts/setup-excalidraw-runtime.sh). ~18MB, 14MB of it fonts.
# NOTE: excalidraw ALWAYS appends its esm.sh fallback to the candidate list, so
# an incomplete mirror here does not 404 — it silently resumes fetching from the
# internet. Never trim it; verify at runtime.
apps/operator/public/excalidraw/
# Vendored Porcupine wake-word model (cdn-egress-fixes-2026-08-02 P-003) —
# fetched ONCE at setup time by scripts/setup-porcupine-runtime.sh, pinned by
# commit sha + checksum-verified. ~961KB, regenerated on install, not committed.
apps/operator/public/porcupine/
# Stale duplicate docs backup trees under the served internal docs.
apps/operator/public/internal/docs.old.*/

# WI-3336: esbuild-bundled host entry (bundle-host.sh) — built per bg-host restart
apps/operator/dist-host/

# WI-4481: flake-soak "prove it discriminates" fixtures. A flake fix drops a
# KNOWN-FLAKY *.flakeproof.test.tsx next to the code under test and runs
# `scripts/flake-soak.sh --self-test <fixture>` to prove the soak lane can
# actually redden a load-sensitive race. They are deliberately red, so they must
# never reach the tree (CI would go red) — the package vitest.config also
# excludes them from every run except the soak's own self-test.
**/*.flakeproof.test.ts
**/*.flakeproof.test.tsx

# Whisper voice-service scratch recordings. The local whisper service writes an
# 8-byte probe .wav into its runtime CWD (packages/operator-core) on each
# invocation and never cleans them up; git-sync's blanket `git add -A` was
# committing the junk and re-dirtying the tree continuously, which blocks every
# release cut (release-local.sh refuses a -dirty superproject). Ignore them.
whisper-server-*.wav

# WI-4776: a browser-extension probe (claude-in-chrome setup tooling, external to
# this repo) creates a temp `probehome.<random>/` HOME-probe directory at the repo
# root containing REAL machine paths (NativeMessagingHosts manifests with this
# box's actual $HOME baked in). git-sync's blanket `git add -A` committed one of
# these on 2026-07-13 and it sat tracked in the tree leaking a real home path
# until removed — the same identity-leak CLASS check-no-box-identity.mjs /
# check-no-identity-literals.mjs exist to prevent, just via an untracked-junk path
# instead of authored source. Ignore the whole class so it can never recur.
probehome.*/

# Playwright MCP session snapshots — agent browser-session debris, never source.
# Carried owner-identity UI text into the 0.0.12 cut (WI-4776 lint); keep untracked.
.playwright-mcp/

# AppImage extractions (`--appimage-extract`) unpack the ENTIRE bundled app: a
# 90MB libwebkit2gtk .so, 64MB corestore .sst files, zellij/kopia binaries, a
# 75MB git bundle. A perf test left one at tools/perf-test/wdio/.appimage-extract
# on 2026-07-20 and git-sync's blanket `git add -A` committed 2.26 GB of it
# (46c2a163d6), pushing the pot-git publish guard's new-bytes total to 2301 MB —
# past its 500 MB cap. The guard then refused EVERY publish, and since its
# baseline only advances THROUGH a successful publish, the refusal was
# self-perpetuating: deleting the files 10 minutes later did nothing (the blobs
# stay reachable from a commit inside the judged range) and origin/staging sat
# frozen for 5 days. Never source — ignore the whole class so it cannot recur.
**/.appimage-extract/
**/squashfs-root/

# Composed rig-VM sidecar — build OUTPUT, never source. `bin/vm-rig/
# compose-rig-sidecar-current.sh` defaults its OUT to $REPO_ROOT/.rig-sidecar-current
# (dot-prefixed, so it is easy to miss in a status), and every run re-emits a
# 58MB esbuild bundle plus verbatim COPIES of all ~549 db-sql migrations and the
# prompts tree. git-sync's blanket `git add -A` then committed 762 files of it on
# 2026-07-26, and logged the oversize warning
#   "EXCLUDED oversized file(s) … they will never push: .rig-sidecar-current/serve.mjs (58.1MB)"
# on every single tick. Same class as the .appimage-extract entry above — a
# regenerable build artifact landing in the tree because nothing ignored it.
# Regenerate it any time with the compose script; it must never be tracked.
.rig-sidecar-current/

# GitNexus code-graph index — a regenerable ARTIFACT, never source. Same class as
# the two entries above, and armed the same way: `npx gitnexus analyze` (the setup
# step libs/papercusp/plugins/gitnexus-bridge's README tells you to run once per
# repo) writes its whole graph DB to <repo>/.gitnexus/, and nothing ignored it. A
# 121-file repo's index is already 27MB; this tree has ~11k tracked TS/TSX files,
# so the first analyze here would hand git-sync's blanket `git add -A` an index
# orders of magnitude past the pot-git publish guard's 500MB cap — the exact
# self-perpetuating freeze documented in the .appimage-extract entry above.
# Ignored BEFORE the first index rather than after (WI-6445).
.gitnexus/

# V8 heap snapshots — a DIAGNOSTIC artifact, never source. Same class as the
# entries above, but arriving from a different direction: they are written by
# hand during a memory investigation (`--heapsnapshot-signal`, the inspector's
# "take heap snapshot", or a heapdump call), land wherever the process's cwd
# happened to be — usually the repo ROOT — and are named for the timestamp, so
# each one is a NEW path that no previous ignore covers. A single snapshot of a
# process this size is ~131MB, past GitHub's 100MB limit, so git-sync excludes it
# and broadcasts "EXCLUDED oversized file(s) … they will never push" to the whole
# fleet on EVERY tick for as long as it sits there (observed 2026-07-27 for
# Heap.20260727.161321.85110.0.001.heapsnapshot, 130.6MB).
# Ignoring the PATTERN rather than the file matters here: the next investigation
# writes a differently-named snapshot and would re-arm the same fleet-wide noise.
# Note this only silences git — the snapshot still occupies disk, and is still
# its author's to delete when the investigation is done (WI-6463).
*.heapsnapshot

# Console liveness markers — per-PID, per-MACHINE runtime state, never source.
# `console-spawn.ts:372` opens every console with `touch .papercup-console-active.$$`
# and a `trap 'rm -f …' EXIT`, so the marker names the live console's pid and is how
# a leftover window's pid is recovered after its agent exits. The trap only runs on a
# CLEAN exit: a console killed by SIGKILL (or lost with the host) leaks its marker
# forever, and each leak is a NEW path named for a pid that no previous ignore covers
# — the same pattern-not-path argument as the heapsnapshot entry above.
# Nothing ignored them, so git-sync's blanket `git add -A` has been committing them:
# 689 zero-byte markers were tracked as of 2026-08-18, 3 of them added in the
# preceding 24h, i.e. slow unbounded growth in the shared tree's file count.
# Ignoring only stops NEW ones — the 689 already tracked need a `git rm --cached`,
# deliberately NOT done here: that is a 689-file DELETION commit, and the 2026-08-15
# incident guard blocks deletion commits from reaching origin while the owner's
# ruling on it is still open (WI-39646). Untrack once that is ruled, not before.
.papercup-console-active.*
